      "value": "A solemn eight second aftermath shot of the deserted Swedish regimental parade courtyard, after the dead soldiers have finally been relieved. The tattered blue banners already hanging on the rear wall slowly slacken and sink down against the stone, their cloth moving once in the last breath of wind and then settling completely still. The courtyard remains EMPTY. Only a few dry leaves drift across the old muster circle. A very slow gentle camera push toward the empty circle, no orbit. Architecture, giant roots, walls and masonry remain absolutely rigid. Preserve the matte dark oil painting brushwork, exact layout, restrained northern light and worn cloth. No new people, no ghosts, no figures emerging, no new banners or objects, no glow, no morphing, no text, no cuts. Audio: distant low regimental drumbeats die away after the first two seconds, leaving quiet wind and a single faint flag rope creak. No speech, no music."
